{
  "title": "TinySID",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Plays C64 .sid music",
        "on a built-in 6502",
        "and SID chip core.",
        "",
        "The tune runs live:",
        "mute voices, bend",
        "the filter, play the",
        "pads with the song's",
        "own instruments.",
        "",
        "Follows the Move",
        "transport and tempo.",
        "",
        "PSID files only",
        "(single SID)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pages",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Mixer",
          "lines": [
            "Voice 1-3: level of",
            " each SID voice.",
            " 0 mutes it.",
            "",
            "Tempo Sync: see",
            " Tempo, below.",
            "",
            "Speed: scales the",
            " tune's rate, 0.75",
            " to 1.5x. Pitch",
            " does not change.",
            "",
            "Est BPM and Key are",
            " readouts: 0 and --",
            " until known."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Tune + Loop",
          "lines": [
            "Line 1:",
            " Loop Len",
            " Loop Start (bar)",
            " Loop Nudge (rows)",
            " SID File",
            "Line 2:",
            " Subtune",
            " Timbre Lock",
            " AutoTune",
            " Master Tune (ct)",
            "",
            "Loop: repeats Loop",
            " Len bars from the",
            " top of Loop Start.",
            " Nudge shifts the",
            " bar line for tunes",
            " with a pickup.",
            "AutoTune: tunes the",
            " song to A=440 and",
            " pulls held notes",
            " onto a note or key.",
            "Timbre Lock: keep",
            " the sound, play",
            " any tune through it."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Mix + Glue",
          "lines": [
            "Spread: 0 mono, 1",
            " voice 2 left and",
            " voice 3 right.",
            "Duck: dip the level",
            " on each beat (the",
            " clock, else the",
            " song's own beat).",
            "DuckRel: recovery",
            " time, 20-300 ms.",
            "FX Duck: the dip",
            " when a sound effect",
            " is hit.",
            "Transpose: +-12",
            " semitones, all voices.",
            "Pump: a low-pass that",
            " closes on each beat",
            " (same beat as Duck);",
            " works on any tune.",
            "LoFi: fewer bits and",
            " a lower sample rate."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Pad + Filter",
          "lines": [
            "Line 1:",
            " Filter",
            " Cutoff",
            " Reso",
            " Chip",
            "Line 2:",
            " Play On Voice",
            " Pad Sound",
            " Pad Mode: Play or",
            "  Control (pads = mute",
            "  1-3, unmute all,",
            "  transpose -/+/0;",
            "  bottom row, lit)",
            " Bottom row, left to",
            "  right: mute V1 V2 V3,",
            "  all on, transpose",
            "  down / up / 0,",
            "  loop capture (press:",
            "  start on this bar,",
            "  flashing; again: end",
            "  here, steady red).",
            " Second row: Notes Out",
            "  per voice (green on).",
            " Top row: the tune's",
            "  sound effects, lit",
            "  purple, hit harder",
            "  for louder."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Notes Out",
          "lines": [
            "Send 1 2 3: send that",
            " SID voice as MIDI.",
            "Chan 1 2 3: its MIDI",
            " channel (1, 2, 3 to",
            " start). Move tracks",
            " listening there play",
            " it. Keep TinySID on",
            " another track.",
            "Pads: second row,",
            " green = sending.",
            " Separate from mutes.",
            "Select TinySID's own",
            " track on the Move",
            " first, or its pads",
            " flash with the notes.",
            "Tuning rides on pitch",
            " bend (+-2 semitones).",
            "SID Delay: hold the",
            " SID back (ms) so it",
            " lines up with them."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Piano Roll",
      "lines": [
        "The first page of the",
        "module. Shows the note",
        "the song's latest voice",
        "is playing. The knobs",
        "here are the Mixer's.",
        "",
        "Top: the song's key,",
        "e.g. [D Min], and",
        "the voice.",
        "Next: note, Hz and",
        "tuning in cents.",
        "",
        "Keys:",
        " Filled white key or",
        " hollow black key =",
        " sounding now.",
        " Small bars at the",
        " bottom of a key =",
        " notes from the last",
        " half second.",
        " Solid black keys are",
        " just black keys.",
        "",
        "All Voices follows",
        "whichever voice",
        "started last."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Song Info",
      "lines": [
        "Each time a tune or",
        "subtune loads, a",
        "silent scan plays it",
        "in the background",
        "(a few seconds).",
        "",
        "It finds the key and",
        "scale, the tempo, and",
        "the instruments each",
        "voice uses.",
        "",
        "Est BPM is a whole",
        "number, fixed once",
        "the scan ends.",
        "Known tunes use a",
        "built-in tempo table.",
        "",
        "Key shows -- when",
        "the tune has no clear",
        "tonal centre."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Transport",
      "lines": [
        "The tune follows the",
        "Move.",
        "",
        "Start: from beat 1.",
        "Stop: halts, and the",
        " voices fade out so",
        " nothing rings on.",
        "Continue: carries",
        " on.",
        "",
        "Loaded while the",
        "Move is stopped, it",
        "stays silent until",
        "you press play."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tempo",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Free modes",
          "lines": [
            "PAL 50Hz or NTSC",
            "60Hz: the tune runs",
            "at its own speed.",
            "",
            "Loading a file picks",
            "the one its header",
            "asks for. You can",
            "change it, and a",
            "subtune change",
            "keeps your choice."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Host Lock",
          "lines": [
            "Locked to the Move's",
            "MIDI clock. A 16th",
            "note is 6 ticks and",
            "the tune's frames",
            "are counted from the",
            "ticks, so it never",
            "drifts, however long",
            "a clip loops.",
            "",
            "Start puts the tune's",
            "first beat on Step 1.",
            "",
            "Lock 0.5x / 2x: half",
            "or double speed.",
            "",
            "Speed other than 1.0",
            "leaves the lock and",
            "just scales the rate.",
            "",
            "If the clock stops",
            "for 2 s the tune",
            "waits for it."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pad",
      "lines": [
        "Play On Voice hands",
        "one SID voice to the",
        "pads. It fades out of",
        "the song and plays",
        "your notes instead.",
        "",
        "Pad Sound lists the",
        "instruments the song",
        "really uses on that",
        "voice, e.g.",
        " 1 Pul50 38 7A",
        " (wave, AD, SR).",
        "",
        "Pulse sweep, vibrato",
        "and trills of the",
        "instrument play on",
        "every key.",
        "",
        "One note at a time,",
        "last note wins.",
        "Velocity sets level.",
        "",
        "The list fills in",
        "when the scan ends."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Filter",
      "lines": [
        "Filter = Song keeps",
        "the tune's own",
        "filter. Cutoff and",
        "Reso then only",
        "offset it, and do",
        "nothing on tunes that",
        "never use the filter.",
        "",
        "Low / Band / High",
        "Pass sends all three",
        "voices through that",
        "filter. Cutoff and",
        "Reso become absolute.",
        "",
        "Chip: 6581 (warm,",
        "rough) or 8580",
        "(clean)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "SID Files",
      "lines": [
        "Put .sid files in the",
        "module's sids folder",
        "(Schwung web manager",
        "or scp).",
        "",
        "Pick one with SID",
        "File on the Song",
        "page. A built-in tune",
        "plays by default.",
        "",
        "Not supported:",
        " RSID files",
        " multi-SID tunes",
        " digi samples"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
